    "narrative": "Our offensive core is anchored today by **Gunnar Henderson**, whose 81.88 efficiency score makes him the premier start of the day. A favorable matchup against Luis Severino, combined with a significant park factor boost and the optimal leadoff spot, gives **Gunnar Henderson** the highest upside in the lineup. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.10) and **Kyle Tucker** (69.90) follow closely, with **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefiting from a strong platoon edge against Sandy Alcantara, while **Kyle Tucker** remains a high-floor selection against Bryce Elder. **Jackson Merrill** (66.44) continues to be an essential piece of our strategy, as his elite sprint speed makes him a high-leverage play for our stolen base needs despite the neutral matchup against Kyle Leahy.\n\nThe decision to keep **Josh Jung** on the bench remains the most difficult call of this slate. With a score of 55.44, **Josh Jung** was squeezed out primarily by the depth of our middle infield and the superior platoon-adjusted projections for **Jacob Wilson** (64.39) and **Brady House** (58.75). While **Josh Jung** offers respectable pop against Jameson Taillon, the optimizer prioritized the specific park-adjusted scoring profiles of **Jacob Wilson** and **Brady House** to maximize our 5x5 production. We are also closely monitoring **Josh Lowe**, whose efficiency score of 48.50 is suppressed by his projected #9 spot in the order; should that lineup slot move up, his value against Spencer Miles would rise significantly.\n\nManagement is flagging several \"Lineup Pending\" statuses that introduce volatility to today\u2019s output. While we have projected standard batting orders, any late-scratch or reshuffling\u2014particularly for **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, who is currently carrying a 57.42 score\u2014could shift our strategy against Jos\u00e9 Soriano. Furthermore, while we are confident in the power profiles of **Coby Mayo** and **Andy Pages**, both rely on favorable park factors to offset their matchup constraints. We will be watching for any weather-related developments in the late afternoon, as our reliance on specific platoon edges means any game delays could disrupt the rhythm of our top-tier hitters.",
